      "lastReply": "My plan · Looking on the web\n1\nLook on the web\n2\nLook for easy treks near Pune with difficulty and\n3\nKeep 5 weekend treks near Pune that fit easy difficulty only, doable in 1 to 2\n4\nCompare difficulty and cost\nAbout 3 minutes\nGo\nChange plan\n7:56 PM\n---\nThe one big ISRO story this week: on Thu 12 Nov, ISRO successfully ground-tested the redesigned third stage (PS3) of its PSLV rocket at the Satish Dhawan Space Centre, Sriharikota.\n\nWhy it matters: The third stage showed problems in the last two PSLV missions, C61 (EOS-09) and C62 (EOS-N1). ISRO then reviewed the whole stage: design margins, raw material checks, assembly and quality tests.\nWhat changed: The nozzle design is stronger, the joints have backup sealing, and the material, assembly and non-destructive testing steps are updated.\nWhat it was not: This was a test on the ground, not a launch. ISRO says more tests are planned after it studies the data.\n\nThis comes from one report (Amar Ujala, quoting ISRO's statement via ANI), and I only saw part of the page. I found nothing else for Thu 5 Nov to Thu 12 Nov, so other ISRO news from that week may be missing.\n\n7:57 PM",
